Lab 1: Installing the IdM Server
Objectives
By the end of this lab, you will be able to:

• Install and configure Red Hat Identity Management (IdM) Server on RHEL 9 • Set up required repositories and packages for IdM functionality • Configure essential IdM components including Kerberos, LDAP, DNS, CA, and PostgreSQL • Understand the fundamental architecture of IdM services • Verify successful IdM server installation and basic functionality

Prerequisites
Before starting this lab, you should have:

• Basic knowledge of Linux command line operations • Understanding of system administration concepts • Familiarity with package management using dnf/yum • Basic networking concepts (DNS, IP addressing) • Root or sudo access to the system • At least 2GB RAM and 10GB free disk space available

